This series adds verification of CPER record headers by consuming the 
xe_error_cper trace event exposed through tracefs. 

It verifies the existence of trace events, sysfs entries and supports
enable/disable control of the trace. It then captures and parses the
trace event generated by querying the get_error_counter netlink API. 

It validates key fields in the CPER Record Header, CPER Section Descriptor,
Intel Public Error Header and Intel Private Error Info.

The tracefs-dependent tests are skipped when the xe_error_cper event is unavailable.

V3:
  - Rebased to align with latest upstream changes of DRM RAS framework
  - Introduced configuring cper_on_query sysfs entry for CPER records
  - Separated get_error_counter() from wait_cper_event() to make tracing more modular
  - Added start_cper_tracing() and stop_cper_tracing() helpers to manage CPER tracing lifecycle
V2:
  - Added support to validate CPER section descriptor fields
V1:
  - Introduced CPER tracefs event format validation, and CPER record header validation

